; node 2: token u$ = lex (src$) — woken by its pushers (fm3 log 103): a push into src$ from a plain function, or its first end, calls the task there

; the scheduler (log 25, 78): the node graph is acyclic, so one pass in producer-before-consumer order settles it — every node its pushers do not wake at the start, and after a push into a stream the nodes it reaches; no trigger can be met while a node runs, so there is no guard, and a trigger that reaches one node is that node's call (fm3 log 103)
